    "summary": "High‑energy NYC show with blistering Crazy Fingers and soaring High Time",
    "blurb": "The Garden night bursts open with a ripping Playing In The Band → Crazy Fingers segue that sets an electric tone. Standout moments include West L.A. Fadeaway, Touch of Grey (early version) and a tight second‑set flow through Estimated Prophet into Throwing Stones. Multiple soundboard sources capture the band in top form.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Madison Square Garden on September 21, 1982 is a quintessential early‑'80s Dead experience – high voltage from the first note to the final encore. The first set launches with a surprise Playing In The Band that rolls straight into Crazy Fingers, giving Jerry a chance to unleash his “liquid lightning” leads while Brent adds funky organ textures. A seamless run through Me And My Uncle, Big River and West L.A. Fadeaway keeps the momentum rolling, and the classic China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue provides the melodic lift that fans love. The second set shines with an early‑version Touch of Grey flowing into Samson & Delilah, then a soaring High Time that segues into a crisp Estimated Prophet → He's Gone stretch before the drums‑and‑space excursion. Throwing Stones and Not Fade Away close the night with relentless drive, while Good Lovin' and U.S. Blues round out an encore that leaves the Garden buzzing. Across all recordings the band sounds tight, inventive, and unabashedly joyous – a must‑listen for anyone hunting that 1982 garden magic.",
